nodecode-you is a rewrite of youdotcom-oss's youdotcom-oss/agent-skills:

  https://github.com/youdotcom-oss/agent-skills
  commit 08f3d80e7ca9518ccc64b38b365a78cc4a762691
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2025 You.com (LICENSE)

The plugin was three MCP server entries (a keyed server, an unauthenticated
free profile, and one each for research and finance) plus five skills:
skills/you-web, you-free, you-research, you-finance and you-discover. This
rewrite keeps the servers' four tools and their argument names -- you-search,
you-contents, you-research, you-finance -- and speaks to the same endpoints
(api.you.com/mcp, its ?profile=free variant, /mcp/research and
/mcp/finance) over MCP's streamable HTTP from the image, through one seam the
tests stub. The skills' routing and evidence rules are the cell's manual
topic, (help :you), and each tool's declared schema is its argument
reference. Nothing of the original is vendored, and no Node, npm or MCP host
is needed.

Left out, and why: you-discover's AI-catalog (ARD) search and its x402
direct-client reference are a catalog-browsing path of their own and are not
among the four tools this cell registers; the MPP/x402 and Coinbase Payments
composition the skills describe need a payment-aware MCP client, which this
cell does not embed -- a keyed account, or the keyless free floor, stands in
its place; OAuth sign-in is left to an API key. You.com and its search,
contents, research and finance services are You.com's; the license above
covers the plugin, not the service.
